    T148
        title        Make Phase 2R Beads feature-scoped with meaningful proofs
        status       done
        priority     high
        derives_from [@plan.Verification.D6, @plan.Verification.D7, @plan.Verification.V8]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.11.48 (closed; task).
            Original title: S02 — Make Phase 2R Beads feature-scoped with meaningful proofs.
            Historical source deliverable: at that time, the user scope was ONLY Phase 2R Beads,
            comprising epic flow-state-e7p.11 and its children. The source required only
            gpt-5.6-luna xhigh subagents for proposal and independent review; its parent owned
            Beads mutations. At that time, preserve each exact
            feature, contracts, dependencies, phase and task-mode boundaries while replacing
            arbitrary implementation/test file allowlists with suggested owner starting points.
            Permit the smallest additional owner, helper, test or integration files necessary
            for the same authorized feature, with a recorded before-edit ownership footprint and
            no repeated permission for routine same-feature edits. Historical excluded scope:
            capabilities, the frozen package, normative contract files, public API gates,
            single-writer ownership and unrelated work. This Beads-only scope is provenance, not
            current Workflow authority. Latest user clarification at that time: tests belong in
            Beads where they provide meaningful evidence, not one new test or mandatory RED per
            Bead. Add or
            change tests for new/changed behavior, regressions or real coverage gaps; reuse
            accepted proofs and current receipts when sufficient. Use test-first RED/GREEN where
            a meaningful executable proof can demonstrate missing behavior; never manufacture a
            failure or redundant proof to close a task. Static/inference tasks may use
            meaningful compile proofs; planning, documentation and verification use appropriate
            evidence. Require orchestrator handoffs to carry referenced stub file paths as
            replaceable guidance separately from production/test edit destinations. Preserve
            historical receipts, closure truth, notes, owners and task states; apply revised
            guidance prospectively to closed tasks. No source, tests, agent-role documents,
            contracts, commits or pushes.
            No editable owner paths were recorded in the source Bead.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: All Phase 2R packets updated with feature-based file
            scope and meaningful proof requirements; three Luna/xhigh partition reviews PASS;
            exact live application and graph validated.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            This completed Beads-only task's historical acceptance was:
            Expected: Every Phase 2R packet uses feature-based scope with suggested starting
            paths and same-feature file flexibility; no outside Bead is modified. Each task has
            meaningful task-appropriate proof obligations rather than a mechanical RED/new-test
            quota. Preserve exact behavioral, inference and integration criteria,
            consolidate/reuse accepted proof where sufficient, and remove contradictory blanket
            RED-receipt requirements and test-count quotas. Test-first behavior proofs remain
            appropriate for actual missing behavior; setup/import failures, redundant tests and
            fake RED are not evidence. Planning, documentation, read-only review, verification
            and receipt tasks retain distinct permissions/checks. The acceptance also required
            preserving historical statuses, owners, notes, closure receipts, exact
            semantic/public/contract/frozen/phase exclusions, file-only stub pointers and
            dependencies. It required validating applied before/after fields, exact Phase 2R
            scope and graph; independent Luna/xhigh review PASS; and export.beads/issues.jsonl.
            Runtime check/build/test commands were inapplicable to this Beads-only task. The S02
            proposal criterion was a compare-before-mutate
            patch and manifest for exactly the source 49-record snapshot, with no outside
            Bead. The source acceptance also called for preserving dynamic subtree scope for
            later reconciliation and reserving approved Beads mutations and exports to its parent.
